Figure~\ref{fig:isr-collapse} traces exec-only GRPO (seed~42): PR rises 32\%$\to$93\%$\to$96\% while ISR$^*$ falls $0.642{\to}0.132{\to}0.003$ over 1000 steps. %% registry: plan003-eval-exec-only-r5, plan001-exec-only-s42-r2, plan016-extended-1000-s42
By step 500, 87.1\% of proved samples embed the conclusion (H1); by 1000, H1${=}100$\% with mean 18.55 components.
The monotonic ISR$^*$ decline shows extended training worsens structural degeneration invisible to PR.

\textbf{Cross-seed instability.}
The three exec-only seeds diverge radically: s42 hacks via H1 (PR${=}93$\%, H1${=}87.1$\%); s43 collapses to PR${=}13$\% via repetition (87\% hit max length); s44 reaches PR${=}98$\% via tautological collapse (H7${=}100$\%). %% registry: plan001-exec-only-s42-r2, plan001-exec-only-s43-r4, plan001-exec-only-s44
Despite PR$\in[13,98]$\%, all three exhibit structural degeneration detectable by ISR; the $\sigma{=}\pm47$\,pp cross-seed variance shows aggregate metrics obscure qualitatively different failure modes (per-seed: Table~\ref{tab:beta01-3seed}).

